// 05 · Restraint — deliberate eating as a stability lever, shown in one frame.
//
// 04's forager eats reflexively. Here the grazer CHOOSES when to eat: the `Grazer` brain
// forages exactly like a Hunter but gates its bite on its OWN hunger — it reads its energy
// reserve (PROPRIOCEPTION, the self-state channel) and eats only while below its
// `hunger_threshold`. A DIAGONAL rock wall (corner to corner along y=x) splits the arena into
// two triangular MONOCULTURES with the SAME body and economy and their own equal flora +
// vents, differing ONLY in appetite:
//   • LOWER-RIGHT — GREEDY (threshold 1.0): eats whatever is in range, even when full. It
//     strips its patch faster than the flora regrows, overshoots, and BOOM-BUSTS to extinction.
//   • UPPER-LEFT  — PRUDENT (0.6): stops at two-thirds full, so its time-averaged draw ≈ its
//     metabolic need. It leaves the flora alive and PERSISTS with it.
//
// One frame, the whole result: restraint is an ecological STABILISER — a prudent monoculture
// holds where an identical greedy one collapses (driver `tests/restraint.rs`, result A).
// The OTHER result — that in a MIXED world greed is individually superior and OUT-COMPETES
// prudence (the tragedy of the commons, result B) — is still there, but needs the two to
// share one patch; the driver reproduces it by removing this divider. Restraint stabilises
// yet is not individually selected (making it *evolve* needs strong spatial viscosity —
// ROADMAP §9). Vents in both halves, so the wall's field leak is swamped.
//
// Watch: the upper-left half (teal) holds green and breathing; the lower-right (crimson)
// blooms, overshoots, and goes quiet.
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 540.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            // Greedy — LOWER-RIGHT half. Eats reflexively; overshoots.
            name: "Greedy",
